    {
      "id": "cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-bgc-units-per-volume.md",
      "sha256": "30d729792e1986dd91c822785512ceabe336ef10a47f0a7db602802e5425d70b",
      "reason": "The question states oxygen concentrations and thresholds are in micromoles per kilogram, while this fragment says CMIP6 o2 is stored per unit volume, so conversion is required before applying the 20 and 60 thresholds or comparing with WOA23.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Convert model `o2` from mol m-3 to µmol kg-1 before applying the 20/60 µmol kg-1 thresholds, using in-situ density from `compute_potential_density_anomaly` (`ref_pressure=None`); `transform_unit`'s constant-density default errs by about a per cent in the deep ocean.",
        "For the oxygen inventory use the native mol m-3 `o2` and `convert_concentration_to_content` (Σ c·volcello), with no density conversion."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "missing-values-and-land-cells",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "pitfalls/missing-values-and-land-cells.md",
      "sha256": "f576244f13dde06fed1777eaa9721c68844f61758f66fac704b44f1551e90df2",
      "reason": "OMZ volumes and oxygen inventories must not let CMIP6's 1e20 land and below-sea-floor missing values enter sums or means.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "xarray decodes 1e20 to NaN; build each field's valid mask from that field (masks differ between variables) and mask weights to the same cells; a hand threshold comparison treats NaN as False and counts land in the denominator.",
        "Use `compute_exceedance_fraction` for the threshold volume so missing cells stay out of numerator and denominator, and keep its returned volume (m3); outputs near 1e20 or 9.97e36 are unmasked fills."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-static-grid-fields",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-static-grid-fields.md",
      "sha256": "2ad0548ca0993fa57d8f1fad27a267dcf9c0e1d007a74343d4bbdbf5b4f1ca17",
      "reason": "OMZ thickness and volume calculations require volcello, areacello and deptho, with layer thickness recovered as volcello/areacello.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "For OMZ column thickness use `cell_thickness_like` = `volcello`/`areacello` (respects partial bottom cells; not `lev_bnds` differences); sum it over cells where `o2` is below the threshold, then locate the maximum.",
        "Threshold volumes and inventories use each model's `volcello`; report `attrs['area_source']`/`volume_source`, and do not rescale a model's area to match another. GFDL-ESM4's `volcello` is time-varying and handled by the loaders."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "omip-weighted-means-and-integrals",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/omip-weighted-means-and-integrals.md",
      "sha256": "89de52676ae54db8f5897bc77a08c78de3f776696db0020935a38b790c302cbe",
      "reason": "Global oxygen inventories and OMZ volumes must be computed as volume-weighted integrals over all ocean cells rather than simple grid-cell averages.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "The mean AOU or percent saturation within the OMZ must be volume-weighted with `compute_basic_stat` `op='volume_weighted_mean'`, with weights restricted to valid OMZ cells; a plain mean is wrong.",
        "A threshold share is a share of ocean volume (m3), not of cells; `compute_exceedance_fraction` returns the amount behind the percentage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "basin-and-region-definitions",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/basin-and-region-definitions.md",
      "sha256": "d0d90c32fab9f6e0a39d4f769a4e902e6412b2ad1b09d9c7d19f6bb3aa426611",
      "reason": "The requested Pacific, Indian and Atlantic OMZ volumes depend on the WOA23 basin partition and on excluding the Southern and Arctic Oceans as separate basins.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Compute Pacific/Indian/Atlantic OMZ volumes with the WOA23 basin mask carried onto each grid (`select_basin`, `load_basin_mask`), folding marginal seas into their parent (`include_marginal_seas=True`) and excluding Southern/Arctic as separate basins as the question specifies.",
        "For named-ocean volumes use surface labels through the column (`depth_dependent=False`); `depth_dependent=True` is for water-mass analysis. State the mask and folding choice."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "concepts/cmip6-o2sat-and-derived-oxygen.md",
      "sha256": "afe46747641c91aff8ddc9f50165a800a7c64d5d2e39b50e816280d02e59fba3",
      "reason": "WOA23 apparent oxygen utilization and percent oxygen saturation within the OMZ use observational solubility formulas and mass units, not the models' o2sat fields.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "WOA23 AOU = `o2sat` − `o2` and percent saturation = 100·`o2`/`o2sat`; the volume basis cancels in percent saturation but not in AOU, and AOU is in µmol kg-1.",
        "Model and WOA saturation values may rest on different solubility/pressure conventions; treat their difference as including a definitional component, and convert any model AOU to µmol kg-1 before comparison."
      ]
    },
    {
